{
  "name": "SquareBalancesSnapshot",
  "type": "object",
  "description": "ONE shared, whole-database broadcast of the computed Square Balances summary (owner spec Oct 9 2026). The owner device's badge pipeline computes the full summary (card balances, loan/folder math, weekly averages, outstanding/cash/deduct items, delivery credits, payouts, config) and publishes the finished numbers here as a single record; every other device's WS ping pulls the whole record, paints UI instantly and refreshes its IDB mirror, then verifies with its own background compute. Whole-snapshot broadcast by design: no per-item events, no merge conflicts \u2014 one record, one monotonic version.",
  "properties": {
    "payload": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": true,
      "description": "Serialized summary payload (same shape as the IDB square_balances_summary snapshot: Maps as entry arrays) \u2014 byLocId card math, payoutsByLoc, storeToLoc, weeklyByStore, storeNames, dailyRemainingByStore, codOutstandingDetailed (items with patient/store/driver/amount/fees), config, deliveryCredits, payouts"
    },
    "version": {
      "type": "number",
      "description": "Monotonic publish version (Date.now() at compute time). Devices apply a remote snapshot only when this is newer than what they already applied \u2014 this is also the echo guard"
    },
    "computed_at": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date-time",
      "description": "ISO timestamp of the compute that produced this payload (data freshness indicator)"
    },
    "computed_by": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "AppUser id of the device that computed and published this snapshot (owner devices only)"
    },
    "computed_by_name": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "AppUser name of the computing device"
    },
    "computed_by_device": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "UserDevice name of the computing device (e.g. THE-DESKTOP(Editor)) \u2014 diagnostics for the single-compute-host gate"
    },
    "p1": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "PAYLOAD SHARD 1/16 (owner spec Nov 3 2026). The summary JSON is sliced into 8000-character strings so NO field of this record ever exceeds the 10 KB realtime transport limit \u2014 that limit was stubbing the whole payload on every broadcast ('Realtime broadcast for SquareBalancesSnapshot#\u2026 was oversize and got slimmed for transport') on all 8 store PCs every compute. Readers join p1..p{parts_count} and JSON.parse. The record now only ever carries a CHANGE MARKER on the wire; each device pulls this record by id and hydrates its own offline mirror."
    },
    "p2": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "PAYLOAD SHARD 2/16 (owner spec Nov 3 2026). The summary JSON is sliced into 8000-character strings so NO field of this record ever exceeds the 10 KB realtime transport limit \u2014 that limit was stubbing the whole payload on every broadcast ('Realtime broadcast for SquareBalancesSnapshot#\u2026 was oversize and got slimmed for transport') on all 8 store PCs every compute. Readers join p1..p{parts_count} and JSON.parse. The record now only ever carries a CHANGE MARKER on the wire; each device pulls this record by id and hydrates its own offline mirror."
    },
